comparison view surface produced by the Dashboard comparison work; same surface, consumer side. |\n45\t| E002 → E003 | 13 (build-against artifact) | The registry UI entry point builds against the run-lineage data model exposed on model versions (an API/data-structure artifact, not a configuration reference). |\n46\t| E001 → E004 | 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the built comparison workflow. |\n47\t| E002 → E004 | 11 (docs last) | Documentation covers the registry-side workflow. |\n48\t| E003 → E004 | 11 (docs last) | Documentation covers opening a comparison from the registry. |\n49\t| E001 ∥ E002 (no edge) | 14 (different repos, no shared artifacts) | Dashboard (odh-dashboard) and Model Registry (model-registry) are separate components and repos with no shared artifacts — they start in parallel. |\n50\t\n51\tNo Investigation epics: the strategy declares no open questions, conditional\n52\tADRs, or pending reviews. The concrete linkage mechanism on model versions\n53\t(custom properties vs. another supported mechanism) is an implementation\n54\tdetail for the Model Registry team, captured as an acceptance criterion, not\n55\ta genuine unknown — it does not change which epics exist or what they do.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n58\t\n59\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n60\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n61\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 | Side-by-side comparison of ≥2 runs in the Dashboard. |\n62\t| HLR-2 | P1 | E002, E003 | Split along component/team boundary: E002 (Model Registry) records the run reference on model versions; E003 (Dashboard) surfaces the comparison entry point in the registry UI. |\n63\t| HLR-3 | P1 | E001 | **Bundled (consolidated) with HLR-1 at P0**: the diff view is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run data — one capability, one epic, listed at the higher of the two priorities. The strategy states requirements were consolidated from two customer councils and overlap in wording was kept; spli